message: "If you write about or cite Ghar, please use this information."
title: "Ghar: a private, self-hosted web app for one household"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Varun"
    family-names: "Biju"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Things-Varun-Codes/ghar"
url: "https://github.com/Things-Varun-Codes/ghar"
repository-artifact: "https://ghcr.io/things-varun-codes/ghar"
abstract: >-
  Ghar is a private, self-hosted web app for one family or household: a shared
  timeline of moments with photos and videos, shared lists of songs, movies and
  places, and notes, flowers, coupons and joke traffic tickets sent to each
  other. It runs in Docker, people join by invitation only, and photos stay on
  the owner's disk by default. "Ghar" is the Hindi and Urdu word for home.
keywords:
  - self-hosted
  - household
  - family
  - laravel
  - inertiajs
  - react
  - postgresql
  - pwa
  - docker
